#: ../../../filesystems/erofs.rst:147
msgid ""
"When CONFIG_EROFS_FS_BACKED_BY_FILE is enabled, EROFS file-backed images can "
"be mounted directly without a loopback block device.  The backing file can "
"be given either as a path, or as an already-opened file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/erofs.rst:151
msgid ""
"When a file descriptor is used, the kernel resolves its path and records it "
"so that /proc/mounts and similar interfaces can still report the mount "
"source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/erofs.rst:155
msgid ""
"Only regular files are accepted as backing files; to mount an image that "
"resides on a block device, use the traditional block device mount path "
"instead."
